  "source_ref": "Altera Agilex 5 FPGA E-Series 065B Modular Development Kit production schematics: carrier board 150-330724-B1 rev 2.1 (FMC+ connector J7 sheet 25, B2B primary connector J9 sheet 9) and modular/SoM board agilex-5e-mdevkit-som-sch-v2p1 (B2B connector J14 sheet 48, Agilex 5 symbol sheets 13 HSIO bank 2A and 17 GTS banks 1A/1B). The FMC site is on the carrier, so every signal is a two-hop join: FMC pin -> carrier net -> B2B pin -> SoM net -> FPGA ball; all 102 chained with no ambiguous or broken links. Grid-checked: all 204 connector pads carrying a canonical VITA name sit on their VITA 57.1/57.4 position (0 mismatches), and 94 pad<->carrier-net pairs agree with the net-name decode (0 mismatches). Cross-checked against UG 820977 rev 2026.07.30 Figure 57, which confirms GBTCLK0_M2C from J7.D4/D5 into transceiver bank 1B and GBTCLK1_M2C from J7.B20/B21 into bank 1A. Note the UG's connector table is offset by one row and names the FMC connector J14; the schematic shows it is J7. Population: the LA pairs pass through 0-ohm 0201 series resistors and the connector sheet carries no DNI markers, so every route recorded here is default-populated. GBTCLK0 additionally passes through the Si549 clock mux (clk_mux_6_sel, EU21) that can substitute an on-board 100 MHz oscillator for the mezzanine clock; the FMC path is one mux selection. Excluded: HA/HB (no HA/HB nets exist on the carrier at all); FMC I2C (I2C_FMC_SCL/SDA_3V3 reach B2B pins D54/D56, which have no SoM-side net - they terminate at the carrier BMC, not the FPGA); PRSNT/PG (never reach the B2B); LA31-LA33 and CLK2/CLK3_BIDIR (not routed); VREF and VADJ per repo convention.",
